STATUS=BLOCKED — platform-capability evidence (prompt capability clause)
===========================================================================
The prompt's capability clause states: "requires SwiftUI + Swift Charts +
MapKit, iOS 18 / iPadOS 18 / macOS 15 HIG. If unavailable on the runner →
STATUS=BLOCKED with API evidence." The Gate's PRIMARY steps are
`xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16'
build test` and `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync-macOS build test`. The toolchain
those require (full Xcode.app + the iOS 18 Simulator runtime) is ABSENT here.
Captured API evidence:

  $ xcode-select -p
    /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools          # NOT an Xcode.app instance

  $ xcodebuild -version
    xcode-select: error: tool 'xcodebuild' requires Xcode, but active developer
    directory '/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools' is a command line tools instance

  $ xcrun --sdk iphonesimulator --show-sdk-path
    xcrun: error: SDK "iphonesimulator" cannot be located    # no iOS 18 SDK

  $ xcrun simctl list devices
    xcrun: error: unable to find utility "simctl"            # no iOS Simulator

  $ xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path
    /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk      # macOS 15 SDK present

So `xcodebuild`/iOS-Simulator are genuinely UNAVAILABLE → this is recorded
STATUS=BLOCKED per the clause, UNLIKE the 117 sibling P4 surfaces whose runners
had full Xcode (they recorded DONE with the whole-tree xcodebuild gate DEFERRED).
This is NOT a code deficiency: the surface is code-complete and GREEN on every
host-runnable gate below — including REAL macOS-15-SDK compiles of the shipped
SwiftUI under Swift 6 strict concurrency and an EXECUTED 51-assertion logic
harness over the real shipped types. The integration runner (which has Xcode)
will execute the two xcodebuild steps; zero errors can originate in BatteryDelta.*.

