===========================================================================
PARITY NOTES (web BatteryDelta.tsx → native)
===========================================================================
  • hasData      web `start!=null && end!=null && isFinite(both)` →
                 BatteryDeltaPresentation.hasData (nil OR non-finite ⇒ unknown).
  • unknown      web muted em-dash + aria `battery.delta.unknown` → visibleText
                 "—" (U+2014), tone .neutral (Color.TS.textMuted), a11y label
                 "Battery delta unknown". This IS the web's data-resolved empty
                 state. (A pure presentational leaf owns no fetch, so
                 loading/error/stale/offline belong to the embedding surface that
                 supplies startPct/endPct — same disposition as sibling 0073
                 BatteryPill and the web source itself.)
  • delta        web `endPct - startPct`; sign `+` / `−`(U+2212) / "" ; magnitude
                 `Math.abs`. compact = "—" when delta==0 else `${sign}${mag}%`.
                 Verified "+60%", "−1%", "—", fractional "−1.5%".
  • tone         web `>0 ? emerald-300 : <0 ? amber-300 : --text-muted` →
                 BatteryDeltaTone .gain/.drop/.neutral → Color.TS.statusSuccess /
                 statusWarning / textMuted (theme + high-contrast aware). NaN fails
                 both comparisons (JS parity) ⇒ neutral.
  • pair         web `${startPct}% → ${endPct}%` (U+2192) → "79% → 78%", tone still
                 derived from the delta. Verified.
  • a11y         web `aria-label = t('battery.delta.aria','Battery {{from}}% to
                 {{to}}%')` → positional "Battery %1$@%% to %2$@%%" via the P1/S10
                 facade; raw (not abs) endpoints. Verified "Battery 20% to 80%",
                 "Battery 79% to 78%". One combined element; icon is decorative
                 (accessibilityHidden); tabular-nums → .monospacedDigit().
  • number       web template-literal `${n}` (no toLocaleString) → BatteryDeltaNumber
                 .jsString: integral ⇒ no ".0" ("60"/"0"/"-5"), fractional ⇒ shortest
                 ("1.5"/"12.25"); never grouped/locale-punctuated. Verified.
  • icon         lucide <Battery> (decorative) → SF Symbol "battery.100"
                 (accessibilityHidden), matching the sibling battery surfaces.
  • testId       web `data-testid` hook → optional .accessibilityIdentifier
                 (applied only when supplied).

